<title>JAPAN: Japan says bans Taiwan pork imports due to disease.</title>
<headline>Japan says bans Taiwan pork imports due to disease.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Agriculture Ministry said on Friday that Japan had banned pork imports from Taiwan indefinitely due to an outbreak of foot and mouth disease.  </p>
<p>&quot;We received a notice on the outbreak from the Taiwanese authorities and decided to ban pork imports from Taiwan indefinitely,&quot; an Agriculture Ministry official said.</p>
<p>Further details of the ministry's import ban were not immediately available.</p>
<p>Taiwan on Thursday banned all pork exports following the outbreak of the highly contagious foot and mouth disease in its hog population, spelling huge losses for one of the island's export industries. Japan is one of the top buyers of Taiwanese pork, which it uses mainly for making sausage.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
